# Support documentation

When a change affects user-visible behaviour, update the matching support doc in the same change, then rebuild the bundle.

| Change | Update |
| --- | --- |
| Screen, label, or workflow | `docs/user-guide.md`, `docs/FAQ.md` |
| Setting, default, or storage path | `docs/configuration.md` |
| Limit, IPC, or error code | `docs/reference.md` |
| New or changed error text | `docs/troubleshooting.md`, `docs/reference.md`, `docs/FAQ.md` |
| Sync, playback, or filter rules | user guide, reference, FAQ, troubleshooting |
| Install or Google setup step | `docs/getting-started.md` |
| Removed feature | Delete the instructions; note it in `docs/roadmap.md` only if a decision records it |
| Deferred vs shipped | `docs/product.md` and `docs/roadmap.md` |

Then run `npm run docs:bundle`. Do not hand-edit `AI-SUPPORT.md`.

`npm run docs:check` must pass: it compares `AI-SUPPORT.md` to the sources and checks that `README.md` links to `AI-SUPPORT.md`. It must not rewrite files.

Leave engineering specs (`PRODUCT_SPEC.md`, `DECISIONS.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`) accurate when a product lock changes. Do not overwrite `ARCHITECTURE.md` by adding a case-variant `architecture.md` (Windows). Support architecture is `docs/app-architecture.md`.

Do not invent features in the FAQ. Source code wins over these docs.
